      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. regarding the nigerian side of things, is the difficulty with trust more about the specific legal/regulatory framework there, or is it more about the general culture of how business gets done in that part of the world?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The difficulty with trust in Nigeria can be attributed to both aspects. On one hand, the legal and regulatory frameworks can be challenging due to bureaucratic complexities and corruption that might deter trust. It must be noted that some regions within Nigeria have made efforts to improve their legal frameworks and business regulations, but progress varies.\n\nOn the other hand, the general business culture in certain areas may still emphasize relationships, negotiations, and personal connections over formal contracts. This stems from historical practices where trust and personal rapport had greater significance. While formalization is on the rise in some business circles, this can take time, especially in smaller, more traditional sectors.\n\nCombining awareness of these factors with due diligence, patience, and building strong local partnerships can help mitigate risks and establish a trustworthy business relationship in Nigeria.",
